@meta
id: 12-16
title: Drill — search, land on the end
chapter: 12
type: drill
skills: search-offset
par: 28
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: find it, click after the 30, type two zeros
open: docker-compose.yml

@brief
Eight times: the worker's `--timeout=30` should be `--timeout=3000`. The
flag is in the middle of a long command line, so the end of the line is
no help to you.

One search with an offset, two characters typed, save.

@keys
| `/text/e` `Enter` | land on the last character of the match |
| `a` | append after the cursor |

@hints
Search for the flag and its value together, and ask the search to leave
you at the end of what it found.
--
`/timeout=30/e` `Enter` puts the cursor on the `0`. Then `a00` `Esc`.

@solution
/timeout=30/e<Enter>  a00<Esc>  :wq<Enter>

Twenty-two keystrokes, and none of them were aimed. This is the
everyday use of `/e`: a value buried in the middle of a line, where `$`
takes you too far and counting `w`s takes thought.

By rep eight the `/e` should be arriving as part of the pattern rather
than as an afterthought. That is the point — the offset is not an extra
step, it is part of saying where you want to be.

@start docker-compose.yml
version: '3.9'

services:
  order-api:
    image: registry.internal/order-api:2.4.1
    command: node dist/server.js --port 4000 --metrics
    environment:
      DATABASE_URL: mysql://database:3306/orders
      RABBIT_URL: amqp://rabbit-1:5672/payments
    depends_on:
      - database
      - rabbit-1

  order-worker:
    image: registry.internal/order-worker:2.4.1
    command: node dist/worker.js --queue payments --timeout=30 --retries=2
    environment:
      DATABASE_URL: mysql://database:3306/orders
    depends_on:
      - database

  database:
    image: mysql:8.4
    command: --default-authentication-plugin=caching_sha2_password

@expected docker-compose.yml
version: '3.9'

services:
  order-api:
    image: registry.internal/order-api:2.4.1
    command: node dist/server.js --port 4000 --metrics
    environment:
      DATABASE_URL: mysql://database:3306/orders
      RABBIT_URL: amqp://rabbit-1:5672/payments
    depends_on:
      - database
      - rabbit-1

  order-worker:
    image: registry.internal/order-worker:2.4.1
    command: node dist/worker.js --queue payments --timeout=3000 --retries=2
    environment:
      DATABASE_URL: mysql://database:3306/orders
    depends_on:
      - database

  database:
    image: mysql:8.4
    command: --default-authentication-plugin=caching_sha2_password
